{"name":"Citrus Peel","hex":"#b7bb6b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"citrus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Any of several shrubs or trees of the genus Citrus in the family Rutaceae.","The fruit of such plants, generally spherical, oblate, or prolate, consisting of an outer glandular skin (called zest), an inner white skin (called pith or albedo), and generally between 8 and 16 sectors filled with pulp consisting of cells with one end attached to the inner skin. Citrus fruits include orange, grapefruit, lemon, lime, and citron."]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Of, relating to, or similar to citrus plants or fruit."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/citrus"},{"term":"peel","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To remove the skin or outer covering of.","To remove something from the outer or top layer of."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The skin or outer layer of a fruit, vegetable, etc.","The action of peeling away from a formation."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/peel"}],"entries":[{"title":"Peel (fruit)","blocks":[{"text":"Peel, also known as rind or skin, is the outer protective layer of a fruit or vegetable which can be peeled off. The rind is usually the botanical exocarp, but the term exocarp also includes the hard cases of nuts, which are not named peels since they are not peeled off by hand or peeler, but rather shells because of their hardness."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bf/Orange_zest_and_peel.jpg/330px-Orange_zest_and_peel.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Peel_(fruit)"},{"title":"Citrus","blocks":[{"text":"Citrus is a genus of flowering trees and shrubs in the family Rutaceae. Plants in the genus produce citrus fruits, such as citrons, mandarins, and pomelos. Many important citrus crops have been developed through extensive hybridization, including oranges, lemons, grapefruits, and limes, all of which have many cultivars."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b0/OrangeBloss_wb.jpg/330px-OrangeBloss_wb.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Citrus"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Chocolate_coated_citrus_peel_01.jpg/500px-Chocolate_coated_citrus_peel_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Chocolate_coated_citrus_peel_01.jpg/1280px-Chocolate_coated_citrus_peel_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/38/Chocolate_coated_citrus_peel_01.jpg/500px-Chocolate_coated_citrus_peel_01.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Chocolate-coated citrus peel.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AChocolate_coated_citrus_peel_01.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Banana_%28partially_peeled%29.jpg/500px-Banana_%28partially_peeled%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bc/Banana_%28partially_peeled%29.jpg/500px-Banana_%28partially_peeled%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A partially peeled banana","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ABanana_(partially_peeled).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7e/Ichangfruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 1x","src":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/7/7e/Ichangfruit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AIchangfruit.jpg"},{